Object.assign(translations.zh.strings, {
  "Cases": "案例",
  "From a model pattern": "从商业模式模式",
  "to a real company.": "走向真实企业。",
  "One well-known company is selected for each pattern. Read the short passage, follow the organizational bridge, then use the official link for deeper context or reopen the pattern in Bridge.": "每条路径选择一个知名企业。阅读简短案例，理解组织桥梁，再通过官方链接深入阅读，或在模型桥中重新打开该模式。",
  "01 · Unbundling": "01 · 拆分",
  "IBM → Kyndryl": "IBM → Kyndryl",
  "Infrastructure separated from cloud, consulting, and software.": "基础设施业务与云、咨询和软件业务分离。",
  "Two different operating logics, allowed to separate": "两种不同的运营逻辑得以分开",
  "IBM and Kyndryl · 2021": "IBM 与 Kyndryl · 2021",
  "IBM completed the spin-off of its managed infrastructure services business as Kyndryl. Kyndryl could focus on operating outsourced infrastructure at scale, while IBM positioned its remaining portfolio around hybrid cloud, software, and consulting. The separation made two different economic logics easier to manage independently.": "IBM 将托管基础设施服务业务拆分为独立公司 Kyndryl。Kyndryl 可以专注于规模化运营外包基础设施，而 IBM 将剩余业务聚焦于混合云、软件与咨询。拆分让两种不同的经济逻辑更容易独立管理。",
  "Bridge logic:": "桥梁逻辑：",
  "infrastructure resembles a Programmed core, while advisory and innovation work need Professional or Project freedom. The new company boundary becomes part of the organization design, and partnerships must recreate the coordination lost through separation.": "基础设施类似程序化核心，而咨询与创新工作需要专业型或项目型自由。新的公司边界本身成为组织设计的一部分，伙伴关系则要重建拆分后失去的协调。",
  "Read IBM’s official case source ↗": "阅读 IBM 官方案例来源 ↗",
  "Open this pattern in Bridge →": "在模型桥中打开此模式 →",
  "02 · Long Tail": "02 · 长尾",
  "A vast platform aggregates many small and niche offers.": "庞大平台汇聚大量小型与利基产品。",
  "One platform, an enormous catalog of niches": "一个平台，庞大的利基目录",
  "Amazon Marketplace · Global": "Amazon Marketplace · 全球",
  "Amazon Marketplace connects buyers with millions of independent sellers, whose products range from mainstream items to highly specific niches. Individual niche products may sell only occasionally, but together they create a vast assortment that can be discovered through Amazon’s search, reviews, payments, advertising, and logistics infrastructure.": "Amazon Marketplace 把买家与数百万独立卖家连接起来，产品从主流商品延伸到高度具体的利基需求。单个利基产品也许销量很低，但合在一起形成了庞大商品组合，并通过亚马逊的搜索、评价、支付、广告与物流基础设施被发现和交付。",
  "a Programmed platform core provides scale and repeatable rules, while independent sellers create Long Tail variety outside that core. The design tension is preserving niche diversity without letting standardized marketplace controls force every seller into the same model.": "程序化平台核心提供规模与可重复规则，独立卖家在核心之外创造长尾多样性。设计张力在于既保护利基差异，又避免标准化市场控制迫使所有卖家采用同一种模式。",
  "Read Amazon’s official case source ↗": "阅读 Amazon 官方来源 ↗",
  "03 · Multi-sided platform": "03 · 多边平台",
  "Users and developers create value through one governed platform.": "用户与开发者通过一个受治理的平台共同创造价值。",
  "A central platform orchestrates a vast developer network": "中心平台协调庞大的开发者网络",
  "Apple App Store · Global": "Apple App Store · 全球",
  "The App Store connects people seeking software with developers who create it. Apple governs distribution, review, discovery, payments, and commercial terms, while developers supply much of the product variety and innovation. More useful applications can attract more users, which in turn makes the platform more valuable to developers.": "App Store 把寻找软件的用户与开发软件的开发者连接起来。苹果治理分发、审核、发现、支付与商业条款，而开发者贡献大量产品多样性与创新。更有用的应用会吸引更多用户，从而又提升平台对开发者的价值。",
  "Apple’s platform stewardship is centrally coordinated, but the ecosystem is distributed. This is a hybrid of a controlled machine-like platform and a project-like developer network. The central tension is how much rule-setting and value capture can coexist with ecosystem autonomy.": "苹果的平台治理是中心化协调的，而生态则是分散的。这是受控的机器式平台与项目式开发者网络的混合体。核心张力在于规则制定与价值获取能在多大程度上与生态自主性共存。",
  "Read Apple’s official platform source ↗": "阅读 Apple 官方平台来源 ↗",
  "04 · FREE": "04 · 免费",
  "Free consumer access is funded by another side of the model.": "免费的消费者入口由模式中的另一侧资助。",
  "Users search for free; advertisers fund the system": "用户免费搜索，广告主资助系统",
  "Google · Global": "Google · 全球",
  "Google Search is available to users without a direct charge. Advertising creates the main cross-subsidy: businesses pay to reach search users through paid results and other advertising formats. The enormous user base, detailed intent signals, and machine-scale infrastructure make the advertising side valuable enough to sustain the free service.": "用户无需直接付费即可使用 Google 搜索。广告形成主要交叉补贴：企业通过付费结果和其他广告形式触达搜索用户。庞大的用户规模、细致的意图信号与机器级基础设施，使广告侧足以支撑免费服务。",
  "the free side grows through scale and automated service, while the paying side requires measurement, sales, and optimization. The organizational risk is letting advertising metrics dominate decisions in ways that weaken user trust or product quality.": "免费侧依赖规模与自动化服务增长，付费侧则需要衡量、销售与优化。组织风险在于让广告指标主导决策，进而削弱用户信任或产品质量。",
  "Read Google’s official company source ↗": "阅读 Google 官方企业来源 ↗",
  "05 · Open model": "05 · 开放模式",
  "Internal capability meets a global network of external innovators.": "内部能力与全球外部创新者网络相遇。",
  "Open innovation turns the company boundary into a resource": "开放创新把企业边界变成资源",
  "Procter & Gamble · Global": "宝洁 · 全球",
  "P&G’s Connect + Develop program invites outside innovators, suppliers, universities, and individuals to help solve product and technology challenges. P&G brings customer insight, brands, testing, manufacturing, and distribution to the collaboration, while external partners contribute ideas and specialist knowledge that may not exist inside the company.": "宝洁的 Connect + Develop 计划邀请外部创新者、供应商、大学与个人共同解决产品和技术挑战。宝洁为合作带来客户洞察、品牌、测试、制造与分销能力，外部伙伴则贡献公司内部可能不存在的创意与专业知识。",
  "open value creation behaves more like a Project network and community than a closed hierarchy. The organization still needs strong gateways, intellectual-property rules, internal champions, and governance so that external ideas can move into commercialization without losing quality or control.": "开放式价值创造更像项目网络与共同体，而不是封闭层级。组织仍需要强连接入口、知识产权规则、内部倡导者与治理机制，让外部创意进入商业化，同时不失去质量与控制。",
  "Read P&G’s official program page ↗": "阅读宝洁官方项目页面 ↗",
  "These are concise interpretive cases, not affiliated endorsements. Official links open in a new tab for further reading.": "这些是简洁的解释性案例，不代表企业背书。官方链接将在新标签页中打开，供进一步阅读。",
  "05 · Cases": "05 · 案例",
  "06 · Atlas": "06 · 图谱",
  "07 · Forms": "07 · 形态",
  "08 · Forces": "08 · 力量",
  "09 · Change": "09 · 变化",
  "See the logic in famous companies": "在知名企业中查看逻辑",
  "Read one selected company for each model path, follow the organizational bridge, and open an official source for further reading.": "为每条模式路径阅读一家代表性企业，理解组织桥梁，并通过官方来源进一步阅读。"
});

